# 5. INTELLIGENT PDF ANALYSIS

Implement a hybrid document-analysis pipeline.

Do not rely on a single detection technique.

Combine the following methods.

## 5.1 PDF structural analysis

Use PyMuPDF and other suitable PDF-processing libraries to inspect:

- Text spans.
- Text blocks.
- Character positions.
- Font information.
- Vector graphics.
- Drawing objects.
- Rectangles.
- Lines.
- Existing annotations.
- Existing widgets.
- Page coordinate systems.

Use pdfplumber where appropriate for detailed text and table extraction.

## 5.2 Computer vision

Use OpenCV and appropriate image-processing techniques to detect:

- Empty boxes.
- Underlined entry areas.
- Table cells.
- Checkbox outlines.
- Radio-button circles.
- Horizontal and vertical boundaries.
- Repeated character cells.
- Form sections.
- Text-entry regions.

The system should distinguish between decorative document elements and actual entry areas.

## 5.3 OCR

Implement OCR for scanned and image-based documents.

Use Tesseract as the baseline OCR engine.

The OCR pipeline must:

- Detect text.
- Identify text positions.
- Preserve reading order where possible.
- Detect labels.
- Recognise section headings.
- Identify instructions.
- Detect likely field labels.
- Associate labels with nearby input areas.

Support image preprocessing, including:

- Deskewing.
- Rotation correction.
- Noise removal.
- Contrast improvement.
- Resolution enhancement where useful.
- Page segmentation.

## 5.4 AI-assisted semantic analysis

Use AI to interpret the meaning of the document and classify detected areas.

For example:

A PDF contains:

"Full Name: __________________"

The system should identify:

- Label: Full Name.
- Field type: Text.
- Semantic identifier: full_name.
- Suggested required status: configurable.
- Suggested maximum length: configurable.
- Position: calculated from the PDF.
- Confidence: calculated from the detection pipeline.

Another example:

"Date of Birth: DD/MM/YYYY"

The system should identify a date field.

Another example:

"Male [ ] Female [ ]"

The system should identify mutually exclusive radio-button choices if the document design supports that interpretation.

The AI must not invent fields simply because they are common in a particular form category.

Every proposed field must be grounded in actual document content or a clearly identified user-created field.

AI-assisted classification must be separated from geometric detection.

The AI should interpret detected content; it must not arbitrarily invent page coordinates.

