# 6. AUTOMATIC FIELD DETECTION

This is one of the most important features of FormForge AI.

The system must automatically identify likely form fields and generate a structured field manifest.

Supported field types must include:

1. Single-line text.
2. Multiline text.
3. Numeric.
4. Currency.
5. Date.
6. Email.
7. Telephone.
8. Address.
9. Checkbox.
10. Radio button.
11. Dropdown/select.
12. Signature.
13. Initials.
14. Text-based table entries.
15. Repeating data fields where supported.

The system must identify:

- Field labels.
- Field names.
- Field types.
- Page numbers.
- Coordinates.
- Width and height.
- Maximum character lengths where appropriate.
- Multiline behaviour.
- Required status suggestions.
- Default values where justified.
- Choice options.
- Related field groups.

## Character-cell forms

The system must recognise forms that use individual character boxes.

For example:

[ ][ ][ ][ ][ ][ ][ ][ ][ ][ ]

It must recognise that these may represent one logical field, such as an identity number or registration number.

It must support both:

- Individual character-cell widgets.
- A grouped logical field that manages the character cells.

This is essential for forms that require information to be entered one character at a time.

Do not assume all text fields are continuous rectangular areas.

## Detection confidence

Every automatically detected field must receive a confidence score.

Use three review categories:

- High confidence: suitable for automatic acceptance subject to validation.
- Medium confidence: requires review.
- Low confidence: requires manual confirmation.

The confidence model must be based on actual detection evidence, not arbitrary fixed scores.

Users must be able to filter fields by confidence.

Provide a review workflow for uncertain fields.

